    "scope": "Bay and adjacent California counties. No verified SF-resident share, so zero SF health credited; not a claim that no SF resident is ever served."
  },
  "decision": "Central and favorable cases exceed $100K/10 Bay QALYs. Separate severe-untreated stress may cross only with a large sustained blood-pressure difference, cheap complete care and stronger additionality; not locally demonstrated.",
  "allocation": "One $100K unrestricted gift: 40% effective BP care course offers, 60% other free-clinic portfolio including acute, other chronic, diagnostic and shared work, health-unquantified but costed. The split is an analyst marginal prior, not provider accounting.",
  "costs": "Annual donor cash cost $350/$200/$700 central/favorable/pessimistic for each of five years. Entire five-year envelope prepaid/reserved from the gift at time0, no interest credited. Includes medication, labs, visits/coordination and overhead within this stream, all failures retained. $200 favorable is an optimistic contextual claim, not verified complete course price. Additional unpaid annual $450/$300/$650 is gross nominal resource stress, not discounted incremental social cost.",
  "finite_health": "Five-year achieved average treatment difference conditional on implementation, inclusive of missed visits, receipt and persistence versus usual accessible care. Only first composite cardiovascular event differences during years1–5 are counted. Event-year first-risk differences discounted, then finite event-specific utility loss or survival flow discounted from event. No lifelong blood-pressure effect. Constant competing mortality applies to all post-event health flows; case-specific extra mortality omitted except fatal first events. Core estimates assume the difference in first events during years1–5 creates durable event-specific consequences, not that every prevented event merely reappears just after year5. Later CVD catch-up is not explicitly modeled. This assumption can overstate benefit. Two calendar-window sensitivities clip every health tail at end of care year5, retaining complete costs and harms.",
  "causal_boundary": "Source RR .80 per10mmHg is trial-meta-analysis anchor; exponentiation across achieved BP differences and application to five-year cumulative risk are modeling transfers. No-new-gift usual-care risks and achieved local differences are judgments. No additional adherence multiplier. Funding additionality addresses activity replacement separately from clinical usual-care substitution embedded in achieved BP difference.",
  "event_partition": "Fatal composite event, nonfatal stroke, nonfatal MI and nonfatal HF shares sum1. Shares refer to avoided FIRST events, not all diagnoses; death not counted again as nonfatal injury. Mortality curve is finite, not sourced lifetime QALYs. Stroke source EQ-5D supports scale only, not causal no-stroke utility or all CVD events.",
  "geography": "Global means all counted US health. Bay includes SF; Monterey and Santa Cruz excluded from nine-county Bay. .85/.95/.70 Bay shares are unmeasured resident allocation priors, not clinic-count ratios; all SF shares0 pending evidence.",
  "funding_overlap": "Most medications and physician/lab/space support can be donated; add resource value, do not duplicate cash item. Current medication dispensing varies by clinic, Northern Peninsula lists prescriptions but not medications. Public coverage/other free clinics remain baseline. Operation Access referral partnership surgery benefits excluded entirely.",
  "harm": "Shared harm per offered five-year course is an all-recipient present-valued health decrement before funding additionality, independent donor harm is a gift-specific health loss even at zero additionality. Same regional share applied explicitly. No monetary opportunity-cost subtraction.",
